.TH GIT-BACKDATE 1 "2025-01-06" "Git External Commands" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-backdate \- Create backdated commits with work hour validation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git backdate
[\fB--overtime\fR]
.I <YYYY-MM-DD>
.I <HH:MM>
.I <message>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-backdate
is a Git external command that creates commits with custom backdated timestamps
while enforcing realistic work patterns. Designed for LLM agents to maintain
organic commit histories.
.PP
This command is discoverable via
.B git help -a
under "External commands".
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I <YYYY-MM-DD>
Commit date (e.g., 2025-01-15)
.TP
.I <HH:MM>
Commit time (e.g., 09:23)
.TP
.I <message>
Commit message
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --overtime
Allow commits outside regular work hours or on weekends
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help message
.SH VALIDATION RULES
.TP
.B 1. Time Sequence
Commits must be at least 1 minute after the last commit
.TP
.B 2. Work Hours
Regular commits allowed 08:00-19:00 (Mon-Fri only). Use
.B --overtime
flag for commits outside these hours or on weekends.
.TP
.B 3. Organic Timing
Minutes cannot be :00, :15, :30, or :45. Valid examples: :07, :23, :38, :52.
Seconds are automatically randomized (1-59).
.TP
.B 4. Staged Files
Files must be staged with
.B git add
before committing
.SH OUTPUT
After successful commit, displays:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
List of committed files
.IP \(bu 2
Commit datetime with random seconds
.IP \(bu 2
Remaining unstaged/untracked files (if any)
.IP \(bu 2
Working tree status
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Regular work hour commit:
.RS
.nf
git backdate 2025-01-15 09:23 "Add user authentication"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Weekend overtime work:
.RS
.nf
git backdate --overtime 2025-01-18 14:17 "Fix critical bug"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Late evening work:
.RS
.nf
git backdate --overtime 2025-01-15 20:42 "Deploy hotfix"
.fi
.RE
.SH ERRORS
The tool will reject commits that:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Are before or within 1 minute of the last commit
.IP \(bu 2
Use quarter-hour times (:00, :15, :30, :45)
.IP \(bu 2
Are on weekends without --overtime flag
.IP \(bu 2
Are outside 08:00-19:00 without --overtime flag
.IP \(bu 2
Have no staged files
.RE
.PP
All errors include helpful suggestions for valid alternatives.
.SH LLM INTEGRATION NOTES
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Always check the last commit date with
.B git log -1 --format=%cd --date=format:"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M"
.IP \(bu 2
Add realistic development time based on the complexity of changes
.IP \(bu 2
Use non-quarter hour times (vary minutes: :07, :23, :38, :52, etc.)
.IP \(bu 2
Stage files first with
.B git add
before calling
.B git backdate
.IP \(bu 2
Review the output to understand what files remain uncommitted
.RE
.SH INSTALLATION
Place
.B git-backdate
executable in your PATH (e.g., ~/dotfiles/bin/.local/bin/).
Git will automatically discover it as an external command.
.PP
Verify installation:
.RS
.nf
git help -a | grep backdate
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-add (1),
.BR git-commit (1),
.BR git-log (1)
.PP
Git external commands documentation:
.B git help -a
.SH AUTHOR
Created for maintaining organic commit histories with LLM agents.
